    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>There is a quiet scandal at the heart of the luxury perfume industry. Walk into any high-end department store and you will see 50ml bottles retailing between $250 and $450. The packaging is heavy, the glass is cut like crystal, and the marketing campaign features a Hollywood celebrity gazing moodily across an empty beach.</p><p>What nobody at the beauty counter will tell you is what is actually inside that bottle. The raw fragrance oil—the compound that creates the scent—typically accounts for less than 5% of the retail price. The rest is marketing budgets, licensing agreements, department store real estate, and exorbitant wholesale margins.</p>"
      }
    },
